# Build context filter for the api and web images.
#
# The build context is the repository root (both Dockerfiles need the lockfile
# and every workspace manifest), so this file is what keeps the context from
# shipping several hundred megabytes of node_modules to the daemon on every
# build. Anything reproducible from source is excluded and rebuilt inside the
# image.

# Dependencies and build output: reinstalled and rebuilt in the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo
storybook-static
**/storybook-static

# The Prisma client is generated inside the image from schema.prisma. A host
# copy is built for the host's platform and libc, so copying it in would ship a
# macOS or glibc engine into an Alpine image.
packages/database/src/generated

# Secrets and local state. .env is the one file that must never enter an image
# layer: layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# Operational data written next to the repository by the backup scripts.
backups
.tmp

# Test, docs and tooling output that no runtime stage reads.
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
docs
*.md
!apps/*/README.md
!packages/*/README.md

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
